column119:
Sure; I was just saying, the parent comment asked for an example of inconsistency there it is.<p>Either allow the use of var to declare a variable, or dont.<p>Dont mix and match in different contexts; this clearly violates the go goal of consistent syntax.<p>Edit, incidentally the use of var is perfectly legal like this:<p><pre><code>    package main
    import "fmt"

    func main() {
      var a = 10
      b := 10

      fmt.Printf("%d %d
", a, b);

      for i := 0; i < 10; i++ {
        fmt.Printf("%d Value
", i)
      }
    }</code></pre>
